      "description": "Hold up your phone above ground in London, Paris, Stockholm or Tokyo and see the metro moving beneath your feet.\n\nSubwhere places the trains under the city in augmented reality. Tilt your phone toward the ground and watch them glide in real time through the tunnels below you. From anywhere, the live map shows them moving.\n\nFour cities in one app, all included: \n\n• London: all 11 Tube lines, from TfL's live arrival predictions \n• Paris: all 16 Métro lines, from Île-de-France Mobilités' real-time predictions \n• Stockholm: all seven T-bana lines, from SL's timetable and live delays \n• Tokyo: all 13 subway lines. Toei's four are live; Tokyo Metro publishes no live train positions, so its nine follow the timetable and are marked as scheduled\n• AR view: the trains through the ground, at their real length, car by car, in their line's colour \n• Track depths reconstructed station by station from published figures \n• Tap a train: line, destination, speed, depth and distance from you \n• Station signs high over every station near you, with platform depths, and track ribbons in each line's colour \n• Camera stabilisation for a steadier picture \n• Ride mode: follow a single train along its run \n• Live map of each city's whole network, from anywhere \n• Next departures from your nearest station, and Home Screen and Lock Screen widgets for it or a station you pin \n• In English, French, Swedish and Japanese \n• Each city downloads the first time you open it, so the app stays small\n\nAR works above ground, where your phone can recognize the buildings around you. Underground, switch to the live map.\n\nNo account, no ads, no tracking.\n\nStep outside, look down, and see the city move!\n\nSubwhere is made by Aesboe AB, an independent developer in Sweden.\n\nSubwhere is not an official app and isn't affiliated with or endorsed by the transport operators or data providers. Each city's data sources are listed in the app, under Data & Attribution behind the info button.",
